  "id": "Compound::DB00678 - Gene::1544",
  "verbalization": "Losartan, a well-known angiotensin II receptor antagonist, is shown to interact with Cyp1a2 through multiple pathways. The evidence suggests that Losartan binds to Cyp2c8, which is involved in oxidative metabolism, and this interaction leads to the participation of Cyp1a2 in oxidoreductase activity. Additionally, Losartan is linked to Cyp1a2 through a different pathway involving the aromatase activity of Cyp2c8. These findings collectively indicate that Losartan influences Cyp1a2 through the modulation of Cyp2c8, which in turn affects the metabolic activity of Cyp1a2. The presence of multiple binding and participation relationships highlights a potential mechanism by which Losartan may modulate Cyp1a2, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of Cyp2c8 in mediating the effects of Losartan on Cyp1a2, suggesting a role in metabolic regulation.",
